## Task: Create a new stack from scratch

When there is no existing branch chain:

1. Use the split map produced by {{.Skill "split-to-prs"}}.
2. Preflight (above).
3. For each PR bottom to top: write code, stage named paths, `["create", "--message", "..."]`.
4. `["submit", "--stack", "--dry-run", "--no-interactive"]` then real submit.
5. Check out each branch from bottom to top. Invoke {{.Skill "pr"}} on each branch to write its title and body to GitHub. After every PR has a number, read the numbers from bottom to top. Append ` (PR x/N)` to each non-sequential title through the `pr` skill edit path, as defined by **Stack position in titles** in {{.Skill "split-to-prs"}}.
6. Mark PRs ready. Share bottom PR URL.

